{
  "type": "fixed",
  "scope": "mymatasan",
  "summary": "Camera credential errors were nearly invisible in the mymatasan UI: `.danger-text` was only ever styled on <button> elements, so the ~25 inline `<p class=\"field-hint danger-text\">` error lines scattered across the app (including a rejected camera login) rendered in the same muted grey as a neutral hint. Errors from the Add Camera dialog, the first-run wizard's add-camera row, and the camera re-auth gate now render through a new shared FormAlert component (warning glyph, red rule, tinted danger-bg panel, role=\"alert\") and the username/password inputs get a red input-error outline, so a wrong password is unmistakable. The Add Camera username field's placeholder also changed from a bare 'admin' (which read as an already-filled value) to a translated 'e.g. admin', and all camera credential placeholders are now italic/dimmed so an example can't be mistaken for a stored value. Separately, double-clicking a live-view tile to maximize it no longer fires when the double-click lands on a control layered over the picture (mute, talk, alert pill, PTZ ring, header buttons); those own their own clicks. The PTZ ring overlay is now pointer-events:none with only its sectors clickable, so the overlay's square corners no longer intercept clicks meant for the tile underneath (maximize and drag-to-reorder work there again).",
  "compatibility": "Backward compatible, UI-only. No API, config, or schema changes. Existing installs pick up the fix on next frontend rebuild; no migration or operator action needed."
}
